Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||12-26-2000||11:25 PM||||The "How To Rebuild Your 60 Degree V-6 Engine" book written by Tom Currao says there was a 1991 model year 60 degree engine with dual overhead cams which makes 210nhp, whatever nhp is. <P>Has anyone ever put this engine in a Fiero. A 210 hp normally asperated engine sounds awfully nice.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||12-27-2000||02:50 AM||||Yeah it's been done a few times.  I'd say it's about the same amount of work as a 3.8 swap.. I think that nhp thing is a typo, from what I remember it's 210 hp and 205(?) lb/ft.  And a 7,000 rpm redline!  I would love to swap one of those in..<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dohcv6.jpg"> <P>Chris West's turbo'd 3.4 DOHC<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dohc_turbo.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Sillhouette.com||12-27-2000||01:17 PM||||The NHP stands for net horse power.  I have heard of the chris west mod have not seen it until now it is quite nice.... is he on this board I don't recall talking to him.  Another Fiero enthusiast that has a 3.4 DOHC engine is Terry K.  He's on this board if you want some more info on those engines they were popular in Wbodies Grand prix Lumina so on you can search a Yahoo club call DOHC and you'll find all sort of info on those engines.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000003||p4n1c||12-27-2000||03:05 PM||||All Cutlass Internationals(Until they stopped the International production for the newer Cutlass line) after '92 have the 3.4 DOHC V6.  That engine moves the car nicely, it's a nice change over the 2.8(125hp) and 3.1(140hp) in the earlier models.<P>------------------<BR>p4n1c<BR>Come out swingin'||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||01-03-2001||11:09 PM||||I drive mine daily with a '97 3.4,fits pretty good,took about a month of weekends,cost about the same as a local,standard rebuild.<BR>Love the way it sounds.||||reg||1
